<title>MALAYSIA: Bank Negara's reserves rise to 70.35 bln rgt.</title>
<headline>Bank Negara's reserves rise to 70.35 bln rgt.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Negara's gold, foreign exchange and other reserves rose to 70.35 billion ringgit as at January 15, compared with 70.03 billion a fortnight earlier, the Bank said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The central bank said its total assets and liabilities fell to 93.91 billion ringgit from 96.74 billion two weeks earlier.  </p>
<p>(In bln ringgit) Jan 15 1997    Dec 31 1996	Jan 15 1996</p>
<p>Reserves		70.35	     70.03		63.39</p>
<p>Assets		  93.91	     96.74		87.71</p>
<p>Currency		22.40	     21.07		18.80</p>
<p>Govt paper	     1.70		3.12		 2.18</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
</text>
